      "title": "PM Modi says cultural connect can guarantee global peace",
      "link": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/pm-modi-address-at-sco-civilisational-dialogue-forum/article71725120.ece",
      "description": "Cultural and civilisational cooperation will strengthen relations among various countries, says Modi at SCO forum; Pakistan Minister to address meet on November 21",
      "source_name": "The Hindu National",
      "published": "2026-11-20T17:37:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Technology created vistas for cultural connectivity, says PM Modi",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/technology-created-vistas-for-cultural-connectivity-says-pm-modi-126112001430_1.html",
      "description": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi on Friday emphasised the significance of holding a dialogue on civilisational connections in India at a time when global discussions are \"dominated by war and unrest\", asserting that cultural connections serve as the \"strongest guarantee\" for world peace.\nIn his address after inaugurating the first SCO Civilisational Dialogue Forum being hosted at the historic Purana Quila in Delhi, he also noted that cultural and civilisational cooperation among member countries of the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO) can further strengthen these ties.\n\"Empires have certainly changed the maps of the world, but civilisational dialogues have changed the ideas of the world and enriched them,\" he said at the forum, attended by delegates from various SCO member countries, including Pakistan minister Musadik Malik.\nA mega cultural programme themed on 'Vasudhaiva Kutumbakum' (world is one family) was showcased to the delegates, depicting the civilisational linkages of .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-20T17:42:05"
    }
